<article class="env-exercise" id="02EI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02EI">Exercise <span data-tag="02EI">111.28.4</span>.</a> Local rings of embedding dimension $1$. Suppose that $(A, {\mathfrak m}, k)$ is a Noetherian local ring of embedding dimension $1$, i.e., </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ k {\mathfrak m}/{\mathfrak m}^2 = 1.  \]
</div>
  <p> Show that the function $f(n) = \dim _ k {\mathfrak m}^ n/{\mathfrak m}^{n + 1}$ is either constant with value $1$, or its values are </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  1, 1, \ldots , 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, \ldots  \]
</div>
</article>